1
00:00:02,060 --> 00:00:02,700
READING

2
00:00:02,700 --> 00:00:04,080
AN INTERVIEW

3
00:00:05,380 --> 00:00:10,340
Pausanias, who was a Greek writer about 2000 years ago, has come on a

4
00:00:10,340 --> 00:00:15,780
magical journey on March the 18th, 2007, to find out about the present

5
00:00:15,780 --> 00:00:16,960
day Olympic Games.

6
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:22,900
He is now interviewing Lee Yen, a volunteer for the 2008 Olympic Games.

7
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:25,480
My name is Pausanias.

8
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:32,160
I lived in what you call "Ancient Greece" and I used to write about the Olympic Games a long time ago.

9
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:37,540
I’ve come to your time to find out about the present- day Olympic Games

10
00:00:37,580 --> 00:00:41,720
because I know that in 2004 they were held in my homeland.

11
00:00:48,200 --> 00:00:50,640
Have you really come from so long ago?

12
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:54,320
But of course you can ask any questions you like.

13
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,300
What would you like to know?

14
00:01:01,920 --> 00:01:06,600
There are two main sets of Games - the Winter and the Summer Olympics,

15
00:01:06,840 --> 00:01:10,520
and both are held every four years on a regular basis.

16
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:15,500
The Winter Olympics are usually held two years before the Summer Games.

17
00:01:16,140 --> 00:01:22,320
Only athletes who have reached the agreed standard for their event will be admitted as competitors.

18
00:01:23,020 --> 00:01:26,120
They may come from anywhere in the world.

19
00:01:28,520 --> 00:01:30,940
How can the runners enjoy competing in winter?

20
00:01:31,480 --> 00:01:32,760
And what about the horses?

21
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:37,980
There are no running races or horse riding events.

22
00:01:38,440 --> 00:01:42,720
Instead there are competitions like skiing and ice skating

23
00:01:42,940 --> 00:01:44,680
which need snow and ice.

24
00:01:47,600 --> 00:01:51,860
It’s in the Summer Olympics that you have the running races,

25
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:56,360
together with swimming, sailing and all the team sports.

26
00:01:58,980 --> 00:02:02,720
Earlier you said that athletes are invited from all over the world.

27
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,860
Do you mean the Greek world?

28
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:12,760
No other countries could join in,

29
00:02:12,760 --> 00:02:14,640
nor could slaves or women!

30
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,200
There are over 250 sports and each one has its own standard.

31
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:32,160
Women are not only allowed, but play a very important role in gymnastics,

32
00:02:32,620 --> 00:02:34,800
athletics, team sports and ...

33
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:41,480
All those events, all those countries and even women taking part!

34
00:02:41,480 --> 00:02:44,860
Where are all the athletes housed?

35
00:02:59,340 --> 00:03:01,640
Does anyone want to host the Olympic Games?

36
00:03:12,780 --> 00:03:18,400
There’s as much competition among countries to host the Olympics as to win Olympic medals.

37
00:03:19,140 --> 00:03:21,980
The 2008 Olympics will be held in Beijing,

38
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:22,540
China.

39
00:03:23,080 --> 00:03:24,060
Did you know that?

40
00:03:26,140 --> 00:03:27,780
You must be very proud.

41
00:03:30,200 --> 00:03:34,920
And after that the 2012 Olympics will be held in London.

42
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:37,780
They have already started planning for it.

43
00:03:38,580 --> 00:03:43,960
A new village for the athletes and all the stadiums will be built to the east of London.

44
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:47,180
New medals will be designed of course and...

45
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:51,980
So even the olive wreath has been replaced!

46
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:53,180
Oh dear!

47
00:03:53,520 --> 00:03:55,480
Do you compete for prize money too?

48
00:03:57,820 --> 00:04:01,000
It’s still all about being able to run faster,

49
00:04:01,160 --> 00:04:03,040
jump higher and throw further.

50
00:04:11,080 --> 00:04:11,780
How interesting!

51
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:14,040
Thank you so much for your time.
